    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0602f0f_3e5bcd51",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 225,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T23:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, Dawn is really the only backend where we need to do this splitting of texture/sampler bindings. Other backends (even those that also lack a combined sampler type, like Metal and D3D) are able to generate the right thing with the old `binding` syntax, so for now I made this a Dawn/WGSL specific condition and avoided introducing a \"current backend\" bit in Caps.\n\nThat said, I would like graphite to eventually use the backend-specific layout flags on all backends since those will enable us to perform validation and catch index conflicts in the compiler front-end, where the rules are slightly different for each backend. If/when we get there, we should generate all layout declarations based on the current backend.\n\nThough that\u0027s a nice-to-have and not really pressing at this time.",
      "parentUuid": "48a43e93_37124e8f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 225,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 225,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "bc38a4ace223e5759bb3610a2309bf1f879f2e5d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8703cb2b_e63aa49d",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 232,
